course: dictionary
lesson: 1031
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Boom is a good example: it can be a noun (a deep sound, or a sudden growth) or a verb (to make a deep sound, or to do very well). The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «A howler monkey booms so loud it fills the building.» Here booms is a verb. The monkey makes a deep, loud sound that fills the whole room. Ask yourself what the sentence is about before you choose a meaning.
explain: «In a boom, jobs are easy to find.» Here boom is a noun meaning a time of fast growth and good times. The words jobs are easy to find are the clue: things are going well.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does "a time of fast growth" fit? Yes, so that is the right meaning here. If it does not fit, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: Boom can be a noun (a boom) or a verb (to boom).
fact: «Boom» means a deep, loud sound, like thunder or a big drum.
fact: «Boom» can also mean a sudden fast growth, as in a baby boom or a boom town.
fact: In sailing, a boom is a long pole that holds the bottom of a sail.
fact: «Boom!» as slang means "There, done!" or celebrates success.
exercise: «A howler monkey booms so loud it fills the building.» What does booms mean here? | *Makes a deep, loud sound | Eats nuts quickly | Sits very still | Climbs the tallest tree
exercise: «In a boom, jobs are easy to find.» What is a boom in this sentence? | *A time of fast growth and good times | A long pole on a sailing boat | A slow, sad time for the country | A loud noise from a cannon
exercise: «The sailor pulled on the boom to turn the sail.» What is the boom? | *A long pole that holds the bottom of a sail | A deep sound like thunder | A quiet, gloomy feeling | A loud shout from the crowd
test: «Business is booming.» What does booming mean here? | Falling down fast | Standing still | Making a loud noise | *Doing very well and growing
test: Which phrase uses boom to mean a sudden fast growth? | A boom of the cannon in the park | *A baby boom | A deep boom of thunder | Booming voice on the stage
exam: Sam shouts «Boom!» after he wins the game. What does it mean? | A long pole on a boat | *There, done! It celebrates success | A deep sound like a drum | Falling down in a heap
